
[1mtacctl scope mgmt-acl lab[0m — per-scope Cisco VTY-ACL + Juniper lo0-filter + WTI IP Tables

Usage:
  tacctl scope mgmt-acl lab list                          Show effective permits for this scope
  tacctl scope mgmt-acl lab add    <entry>[,<entry>...]   Add one or more entries to the per-scope list
  tacctl scope mgmt-acl lab remove <entry>[,<entry>...]   Remove entries (a bare <cidr> removes every entry of that CIDR)
  tacctl scope mgmt-acl lab clear                         Wipe the per-scope list (confirms; render falls back to global)
  tacctl scope mgmt-acl lab cisco-name   [<label>]        Per-scope Cisco VTY-ACL name
  tacctl scope mgmt-acl lab juniper-name [<label>]        Per-scope Junos filter name

An <entry> is a <cidr>, or a <cidr> with the services it permits:
  <cidr>[:<service>[,<service>...]]    e.g. 172.16.100.0/23:tcp/22,udp/161,udp/162
  <service> is tcp/<ports>, udp/<ports> or icmp; <ports> is N, N-M or *.
  A <cidr> alone permits every protocol and port from it (the WTI IP Tables list renders that; a
  Cisco VTY-ACL and a Junos filter list a source only when its entry permits tcp/22).

Current entries: 0 (per-scope) / 0 (global fallback)

